Setting. S and S' are PD (divided power) base rings, with S = k{T} and S' = k'{T} (PD polynomial algebras). A_S denotes the PD de Rham algebra of the PD affine line over S: the PD polynomial algebra S{X_0}, with generators X_0^{(i)}, together with the differential d and the 1-form dX_0. The page studies a morphism of differential PD-algebras phi_1 lying over a base map phi_0. Its aim is to describe all such morphisms, and in particular the automorphisms of A_{S'} compatible with the augmentation.

Step 1. Write xi_i = phi_1(X_0^{(i)}) for i >= 1. Since phi_1 respects the PD structure and commutes with d:
- xi_i xi_j = c_{ij} xi_{i+j}, with c_{ij} the binomial coefficient (i+j choose i);
- d xi_i = xi_{i-1} d xi_1, the PD-derivation rule;
- phi_1(dX_0) = d xi_1;
- xi_i lies in the augmentation ideal S'{X_0}^+.

Step 2. Decompose xi_i = A_i + B_i dX_0 with A_i, B_i in S'{X_0}. This suggests he lets phi_1 be a map of the whole (not necessarily graded) algebra, with dX_0 squaring to zero. Comparing components gives dA_i = A_{i-1} A_1' (where ' is the X_0-derivative) and A_i = A_1^{(i)}. So the whole family is determined by A_1, and in the same way by the divided powers of xi_1.

Step 3 (Remarque). Hence phi_1 factors uniquely as psi_1 o phibar_0, where:
- phibar_0 is the obvious extension of phi_0 (X_0^{(i)} -> X_0^{(i)}, dX_0 -> dX_0);
- psi_1 is an S'-automorphism of the S'-differential algebra A_{S'} compatible with the augmentation.

Step 4. Impose compatibility with the augmentation beta: X_0 -> T, dX_0 -> 0. This forces beta_{S'}(xi_i) = phi_0(T^{(i)}), i.e. beta_{S'}(A_i) = phi_0(T^{(i)}). This holds automatically once beta_{S'}(A_1) = phi_0(T), because A_i = A_1^{(i)} and phi_0 is a PD morphism.

Step 5. So A_1 = X_0 + f, with f in a PD polynomial algebra k{X_0, X_1}. He writes f = sum over i, j >= 1 of X_0^{(i)} X_1^{(j)}. This looks like a universal or generic perturbation term parametrising the augmentation-preserving automorphisms, i.e. coordinates on an automorphism group(-scheme) of the PD de Rham algebra. The sheet ends with 'La remarque ci-dessus se prolonge —'.

Physical note. The neighbouring pages are typescript pages 49-50 of SGA 7 exposé IX (Néron models, Serre's lemma 4.7.1), with unrelated content. Grothendieck was writing on the backs of old typescript.
